      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, the \"evolving threat\" angle is always a good play. But I'm worried the Miller Group's CTO is pretty sharp and will push back. If he asks for specific evidence of these \"subtle breaches\" or \"outdated\" gaps since the audit actually came back clean, what are we supposed to tell him? I don't want us to get caught in a lie if he asks for the data behind that claim.",
